[{:db/id "q-72773/selection/83f419a198a4272ff136d76a7818384354f74655b230bbd8dd8902843f19147a" :answer/id #uuid "53c4bb85-fcfc-571b-bbc2-c491b3bddd2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72773/selection/ff8e59b6a3bd95b580597792451429a20cf15bf51f97b511bc727f34ceee724b" :answer/id #uuid "bcbf3c7e-1e2b-58a3-ab52-ed604d15928b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72773/selection/bda6b54f3d80a63e1e9c0987cbb7548f978de941763590f165916a0977a9fdc3" :answer/id #uuid "17b4ed42-a300-540d-bbe6-9c218749d561" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72773/selection/1469cb3234d8827d90ce635fea976fd9f8898ec812577cad4fcea5557d011275" :answer/id #uuid "ada4277c-692f-5571-8dd7-51ca9653374d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72773/selection/cfd318375d7df7b9f280ebb90f42c57fc82542cc514f7fa9faad33f36c2cb4de" :answer/id #uuid "7762dbc3-1344-5221-8056-60499bebcecc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72773/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac424a1d-e694-5a65-bafd-347332fa85e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72773/selection/1469cb3234d8827d90ce635fea976fd9f8898ec812577cad4fcea5557d011275" :answer-field/choices ["q-72773/selection/83f419a198a4272ff136d76a7818384354f74655b230bbd8dd8902843f19147a" "q-72773/selection/ff8e59b6a3bd95b580597792451429a20cf15bf51f97b511bc727f34ceee724b" "q-72773/selection/bda6b54f3d80a63e1e9c0987cbb7548f978de941763590f165916a0977a9fdc3" "q-72773/selection/1469cb3234d8827d90ce635fea976fd9f8898ec812577cad4fcea5557d011275" "q-72773/selection/cfd318375d7df7b9f280ebb90f42c57fc82542cc514f7fa9faad33f36c2cb4de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72773" :question/id #uuid "cf9f9645-9c31-5537-b299-ec1550429963" :question/math-academy-id "q-72773" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$  what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/00d540b1f6412e4af2617452fbf0c58750d01e844d89d0d92cfacc0cb3e45e32.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72773/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15d21b01-bbad-507d-8b3c-1052ebba30eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72773"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330397/field-1/7ef186fd8b5a1c52c90d35337c0050c3c2cd876fe199bd9866d5167b1165edd0" :answer/id #uuid "e79c6789-9094-559f-b5eb-44a4c969ad78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330397/field-1/608b697f811192589eec3729e28e5d056be7cd5127af1a846d717a33508ae203" :answer/id #uuid "90781274-5356-5a69-ae32-20250f80bf41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330397/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5aad4b5-464a-5256-ac92-540930fdd30c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330397/field-1/7ef186fd8b5a1c52c90d35337c0050c3c2cd876fe199bd9866d5167b1165edd0" :answer-field/choices ["q-330397/field-1/7ef186fd8b5a1c52c90d35337c0050c3c2cd876fe199bd9866d5167b1165edd0" "q-330397/field-1/608b697f811192589eec3729e28e5d056be7cd5127af1a846d717a33508ae203"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330397/field-2/5cf956242b9863bec1345051ca8ccb3caf8118ef7c2e138f555df8faaf61abd8" :answer/id #uuid "71b94733-29fa-5c50-a3a1-da0cac98369b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330397/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "93e3db6d-f7a1-57c9-a97b-038c1c460dda" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330397/field-2/5cf956242b9863bec1345051ca8ccb3caf8118ef7c2e138f555df8faaf61abd8" :answer-field/choices ["q-330397/field-2/5cf956242b9863bec1345051ca8ccb3caf8118ef7c2e138f555df8faaf61abd8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330397" :question/id #uuid "892abfcf-428b-5897-9666-b647328728e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-330397" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, the exact solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}=0,$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$  are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2} & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$\n\nNote that $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is not in the range $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ To get the first solution that's within the required range, we need to find an angle that's coterminal with $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ To do this, we simply add $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/012f0986293e2a4318dc68633a4ac0e91732d74300496427aaaa6635b417efe4.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order,  the solutions are \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,x=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-330397/field-1" "q-330397/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15d21b01-bbad-507d-8b3c-1052ebba30eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330397"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8436/selection/120c4e36fb30a0e2ea284b09bede33667485b47ea01d93e4d89a9a4f2fc6e2d5" :answer/id #uuid "381ed357-d22d-5fc8-bc14-b4a9d49c21a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8436/selection/83f419a198a4272ff136d76a7818384354f74655b230bbd8dd8902843f19147a" :answer/id #uuid "aeffb562-9114-543a-bbe2-1ca914dd8550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8436/selection/ff8e59b6a3bd95b580597792451429a20cf15bf51f97b511bc727f34ceee724b" :answer/id #uuid "01519aff-8466-512f-b32f-c9ab38441858" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8436/selection/0c02d5af3e10330c39a60d040b35a4e42019ef35d23f491906127f3bb8dd87b2" :answer/id #uuid "a1594908-f00c-5217-be7d-a7a74d1f71c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8436/selection/cfd318375d7df7b9f280ebb90f42c57fc82542cc514f7fa9faad33f36c2cb4de" :answer/id #uuid "61532bd5-d33e-5e7a-9cb2-1c9d54fd5ac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8436/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "63a69bd0-ac4e-5632-b30b-bb335315fa7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8436/selection/ff8e59b6a3bd95b580597792451429a20cf15bf51f97b511bc727f34ceee724b" :answer-field/choices ["q-8436/selection/120c4e36fb30a0e2ea284b09bede33667485b47ea01d93e4d89a9a4f2fc6e2d5" "q-8436/selection/83f419a198a4272ff136d76a7818384354f74655b230bbd8dd8902843f19147a" "q-8436/selection/ff8e59b6a3bd95b580597792451429a20cf15bf51f97b511bc727f34ceee724b" "q-8436/selection/0c02d5af3e10330c39a60d040b35a4e42019ef35d23f491906127f3bb8dd87b2" "q-8436/selection/cfd318375d7df7b9f280ebb90f42c57fc82542cc514f7fa9faad33f36c2cb4de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8436" :question/id #uuid "619d6fe2-1442-54ad-8625-6210eaafb0f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-8436" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{2}=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$  what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{2} & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/269d503189ab1027c3d8028542ef0c6a0e2f146aef0f7916691428866ce1b894.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4}=\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{16}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8436/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15d21b01-bbad-507d-8b3c-1052ebba30eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8436"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8431/selection/080aa7aa965688cd2badb7b57dce39c6db33b60e55a0036b313d953319d0b4d6" :answer/id #uuid "9af43ed6-6ed6-5d2e-8bb0-a63019e4c4d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8431/selection/1b3f0146a5831b166327ed16f9e4da83d2605a1946f5f8c3ee6e12d765348def" :answer/id #uuid "6e406ad8-6993-5f37-b1b0-4b56ccc50379" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8431/selection/cf3a880703421bd31bc18810eb34046c2a68ca85847ca52ea34f46125e0d95cb" :answer/id #uuid "5b5b71e2-dab5-5a17-8fc4-92cbf972fd06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8431/selection/470a96bcbac0faed7b874a5281ac63134c4d72d06e2f472fcedac4de46dac31c" :answer/id #uuid "00f3e839-c938-5d78-84d4-a99b51dc0078" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8431/selection/cfd318375d7df7b9f280ebb90f42c57fc82542cc514f7fa9faad33f36c2cb4de" :answer/id #uuid "f34b7938-c0b1-5402-a6a8-3e82d975be90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8431/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4184cc1c-6b9c-510d-847e-5d8d41baec28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8431/selection/cf3a880703421bd31bc18810eb34046c2a68ca85847ca52ea34f46125e0d95cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-8431/selection/080aa7aa965688cd2badb7b57dce39c6db33b60e55a0036b313d953319d0b4d6" "q-8431/selection/1b3f0146a5831b166327ed16f9e4da83d2605a1946f5f8c3ee6e12d765348def" "q-8431/selection/cf3a880703421bd31bc18810eb34046c2a68ca85847ca52ea34f46125e0d95cb" "q-8431/selection/470a96bcbac0faed7b874a5281ac63134c4d72d06e2f472fcedac4de46dac31c" "q-8431/selection/cfd318375d7df7b9f280ebb90f42c57fc82542cc514f7fa9faad33f36c2cb4de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8431" :question/id #uuid "0c3f12b8-0685-5578-a04a-53dba75239e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-8431" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$  what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is not in the range $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ To get the first solution that's within the required range, we need to find an angle that's coterminal with $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ To do this, we simply add $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2\\pi =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/0716b8ab50e525f453ae8bc690d404a150f2da98f0a90b6c8856ae9925e7c515.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}\\cdot \\frac{4\\pi }{3}=\\frac{20{\\pi }^{2}}{9}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8431/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15d21b01-bbad-507d-8b3c-1052ebba30eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8431"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328393/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08" :answer/id #uuid "782b9fca-6fa3-5796-b1a9-015ed90a1631" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328393/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4ecfce4-fc0f-5d9f-a177-795e12cbc771" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328393/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08" :answer-field/choices ["q-328393/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328393/field-2/d569d64e1b94dabdc9f89c1070c848c6c96526a20f320d6b4971ae3a32604bcf" :answer/id #uuid "04221237-988a-510a-b6b7-e472f70baacd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328393/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c043081f-89f3-59aa-aa57-36bb165b0966" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328393/field-2/d569d64e1b94dabdc9f89c1070c848c6c96526a20f320d6b4971ae3a32604bcf" :answer-field/choices ["q-328393/field-2/d569d64e1b94dabdc9f89c1070c848c6c96526a20f320d6b4971ae3a32604bcf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328393" :question/id #uuid "a5954b94-b8cd-5696-a81c-2e44aa692bad" :question/math-academy-id "q-328393" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, the exact solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ are\n\n$x=$ \n{{field-1}}$,\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arcsin\\,(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/d50a4a9f62be8b8af4cc657a5b0ab1547288b844eaa05af1a57ed39b8afa0d6d.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\,x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328393/field-1" "q-328393/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15d21b01-bbad-507d-8b3c-1052ebba30eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328393"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72779/selection/8f99cb30e4e44971e3fdee5f08694f34bc0d938f766dc28c72474059b560086c" :answer/id #uuid "8d63ba89-d1ac-51d5-a2c7-2691d079d5f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={45.9}^{∘},{131.4}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72779/selection/239e37f6a979c1dcdb259a34dd5f1da2697bddb64296be0a663730318a258ea2" :answer/id #uuid "e2b075e9-ecd6-512a-8794-c76962fa23a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={48.6}^{∘},{135.7}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72779/selection/51ab1c5117deb3e1b439aef7d6316c2a9268324ae31485eccbd3a85a46422b5c" :answer/id #uuid "d5faf294-d323-527a-a5bc-54e6da758784" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={48.6}^{∘},{139.1}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72779/selection/c0ed6ca95ac47622eb9f0021b9a161cb96d12286f2ab9e38f7549c15aa8c8b31" :answer/id #uuid "0abfb4ab-4bff-5f5d-b077-54b5d46a7749" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={50.1}^{∘},{131.4}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72779/selection/488f40be609ff9d9e47413b1ca31ee800383e935fe66925388a012f151fb4e2a" :answer/id #uuid "789bd05f-eb7d-588c-aeb0-407986658648" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={48.6}^{∘},{131.4}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72779/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "81f58714-9c66-5ecf-9acb-b5feb9024f48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72779/selection/488f40be609ff9d9e47413b1ca31ee800383e935fe66925388a012f151fb4e2a" :answer-field/choices ["q-72779/selection/8f99cb30e4e44971e3fdee5f08694f34bc0d938f766dc28c72474059b560086c" "q-72779/selection/239e37f6a979c1dcdb259a34dd5f1da2697bddb64296be0a663730318a258ea2" "q-72779/selection/51ab1c5117deb3e1b439aef7d6316c2a9268324ae31485eccbd3a85a46422b5c" "q-72779/selection/c0ed6ca95ac47622eb9f0021b9a161cb96d12286f2ab9e38f7549c15aa8c8b31" "q-72779/selection/488f40be609ff9d9e47413b1ca31ee800383e935fe66925388a012f151fb4e2a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72779" :question/id #uuid "dc66b404-2b99-5ef1-898b-f30b9a1ab25e" :question/math-academy-id "q-72779" :question/problem "Calculate, in degrees, rounded to $1$ decimal place, the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{3}{4}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})=48.590\\,377{…}^{∘}≈48.590\\,{4}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $48.590\\,{4}^{∘}$ lies inside the range, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=48.590\\,{4}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=48.590\\,{4}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=48.590\\,{4}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/4864e26ba05324041220dff99d1929b4c280b77456295d00d13d246279b4e628.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-48.590\\,{4}^{∘} \\\\  & =131.409\\,{6}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions (rounded to one decimal place) are $x={48.6}^{∘},{131.4}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72779/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aecfac4d-b8c4-5591-b623-0fa8c192ac80"] :kno